# Who has to approve what.
#
# GitHub requests a review from the owner of every path a pull request touches.
# With "Require review from Code Owners" turned on in the branch protection
# rule, that review is not optional — which is the mechanism behind "nothing
# reaches main without being read by someone else".
#
# A username here must be a collaborator on the repository, or GitHub silently
# ignores the line. Check with: gh api repos/:owner/:repo/collaborators
#
# Last match wins, so the specific rules at the bottom override the catch-all.

# Everything, by default.
* @Shokhanasser1

# ── The five areas from CONTRIBUTING.md, Part 4 ───────────────────────────────
# Add the second owner next to the lead as people take their areas. Two names on
# a line means *either* can approve, which keeps a holiday from blocking a
# merge. Leave the lead on every line: the lead reviews everything.
#
# 1. Backend & API
#/backend/apps/          @Shokhanasser1 @username
# 2. Frontend & UI
#/frontend/src/           @Shokhanasser1 @username
# 3. Content & i18n
#/frontend/src/locales/   @Shokhanasser1 @username
#/frontend/src/data/      @Shokhanasser1 @username
# 4. Quality & release
#/.github/                @Shokhanasser1 @username
# 5. Research & docs
#/docs/                   @Shokhanasser1 @username

# ── Things that need the lead specifically, whoever else owns the area ────────
# Not because the others are not trusted. Because a mistake in one of these is
# not visible in review of the diff alone — it is visible in what stops being
# true afterwards.

# Settings. The fail-open settings bug turned on DEBUG in production, opened
# CORS to everyone and returned account sign-in codes in HTTP responses.
/backend/base/settings/   @Shokhanasser1

# Authentication, rate limits, uploads, moderation. Every serious finding in the
# 22 August audit was in one of these.
/backend/apps/accounts/   @Shokhanasser1
/backend/apps/chat/       @Shokhanasser1
/backend/apps/validators.py @Shokhanasser1

# CI is what stops everything else. A change here can quietly stop the tests
# running at all, and a workflow that does not run reports success.
/.github/                 @Shokhanasser1

# Migrations are the one thing a shared database cannot take back.
# See docs/TEAM.md — "The database is shared".
/backend/apps/*/migrations/ @Shokhanasser1
